Section name: Introduction
Excerpt:
The Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN) search problem involves retrieving the 𝑘closest points to a given query point 𝑞in a𝑑- dimensional metric space. This problem is foundational in database systems, machine learning, information retrieval, and computer vision, and has seen growing importance in large language models (LLMs) [ 34], particularly in retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) pipelines, where relevant documents must be retrieved efficiently from large corpora [ 18,39]. More generally, any vector database system implements some form of ANN search to enable efficient vector similarity queries [ 4,24,55]. For a comprehensive overview of additional applications, we refer the reader to the following surveys [40, 42, 63]. Several classes of algorithms have been developed for ANN. Hash-based approaches (e.g., Locality-Sensitive Hashing [ 11,26, Conference’17, Washington, DC, USA 2026. A

