Section name: HNSW is a HENN Graph
Excerpt:
In this section, we present one of our main contributions: showing that HNSW is a HENN graph, with a high probability. Building on this connection, we derive probabilistic time guarantees for HNSW. We begin with a simplified description of HNSW [ 46]. During preprocessing, points are inserted incrementally into the index. For each new point, a random variable determines its maximum layer, with the probability of assignment to higher layers decreasing ex- ponentially. After the layers are determined, the point is connected at each layer to its nearest neighbors among the previously inserted points, identified using the greedy search procedure (Algorithm 1). Equivalently, HNSW can be viewed as starting from a base layer containing all points and recursively constructing higher layers by randomly sampling subsets of points, such that the size of each layer decreases exponentially with the l

